{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dear Marie,\n\nWeimar receives me with a warmth that makes me long for Berlin, where you await me. The air here is mild, but my heart remains with our sons.\n\nLunch at Goethe’s was an event. I sat next to him; his wit is still sharp despite his age. Mrs. von Goethe was absent, which somewhat clouded the mood, yet the company was lively. I spoke with him about the state of affairs in France, both in politics and literature. He listened to me, as he does, with that quiet, superior attention. It is interesting how he views things from his own perspective, beyond academic debates.\n\nIn the evening I went to the theater. The play was decent, but nothing remarkable. I am tired, but content. Please give my regards to Karl and Immanuel, and tell Ludwig that I am thinking of him.\n\nYour faithful\nG. Hegel"}}],"created":1795221240,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":190,"prompt_tokens":279,"total_tokens":469,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-Lv8ZmZwwOWTPT5qD0LoZ82CAy82pYSFC","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":279,"prompt_ms":455.387,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.6322114695340502,"prompt_per_second":612.6657107032041,"predicted_n":190,"predicted_ms":4478.58,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.696190476190477,"predicted_per_second":42.200876170571924}}